    <pageContent>
      <Value><![CDATA[{
  "contentData": [
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "a58b29f0-29c6-47b8-b8ce-329b38fbed3c",
      "key": "a42b2cae-fc80-4e94-98ca-104455118345",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "text",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Ch2\u003ECMS and DXP upgrade specialists\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EUpgrading a Content Management System (CMS) or Digital Experience Platform (DXP) to the latest release is something we specialise in. The normal process we follow can depend on whether we built the site, or if it was built by a previous agency.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EHow significant is the upgrade?\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003ECMS upgrades come in all shapes and sizes. Some upgrades can be more significant depending on factors such as major releases, the gap between releases, and the presence of custom code and integrations.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EUpgrade process: Phase 1\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003ETo ascertain exactly what will be involved in an upgrade we always carry out a two-phased approach. Phase 1 is separately invoiced at a reasonable fixed cost and takes between five to ten working days.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EHere a developer takes a fresh cut of the current website and carries out what is known as a \u0022brute force upgrade\u0022. We put the results into a document that details exactly what needs doing, then compile a backlog of tasks.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EUpgrade process: Phase 2 - carrying out the upgrade\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EWe pull down a copy of all the website live databases and create a parallel UAT environment. In the parallel UAT environment we carry out the upgrade, all the testing and remediation of any issues.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EOnce we\u0027ve completed our work, we will then ask you to carry out your own testing. Depending on the testing, there may be further changes required, until we reach client UAT sign-off. Finally, we schedule the actual upgrade to live.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
